content.text:
**Finding submitted: MISSING (critical).**

The Site Development and Hosting Agreement has no limitation-of-liability clause at all — no cap, no exclusion of indirect/consequential damages, and no carve-out framework. I confirmed this by scanning the full outline and both body sections, and by searching "liability", "damages", "consequential" and "indemnif"; the only hits are the no-joint-venture language in Section 10.2. Neither the Fees (Section 3, a 30% revenue share on Net Sales) nor the Termination Payment (Section 4.2) provisions contain any liability limitation.

Because both parties sit fully uncapped and exposed to consequential damages, the document fails even the fallback position (mutual 12-month fee cap with carve-outs for indemnification, confidentiality, gross negligence and wilful misconduct).

The validated redline inserts a new Section 9(c) that:
- caps each party's aggregate liability at the greater of 12 months' fees and USD 1,000,000 (mutual);
- mutually excludes indirect/consequential damages;
- places confidentiality/data protection, indemnification, gross negligence, wilful misconduct, fraud and IP infringement outside the cap;
- confirms the Company's payment obligations are not subject to the cap.

I placed it in Section 9 deliberately: Section 10.7 lists Sections 6.3, 7, 9 and 10 as surviving, so the cap carries past termination without needing a separate survival edit.
